Imports:
  - Types:
      - Manga
      - MangaUpdate
      - MangaWithChapterCount
    From: domain/src/main/java/tachiyomi/domain/manga/model

Annotations: |
  This cell is the storage port for the manga aggregate, the single most-depended-upon
  repository interface in the codebase. It also exposes library-scoped and upcoming-release
  queries that join across manga and category/chapter state maintained elsewhere; those joins
  are the implementation's responsibility, not this contract's.

  Use Manga/`MangaUpdate`/`MangaWithChapterCount` from Imports throughout.

---

"MangaRepository()":
  location: MangaRepository.kt
  annotations: |
    Storage port for the manga aggregate, plus library-membership and duplicate/upcoming
    queries built on top of it.
  methods:
    "getMangaById(id: Long) -> manga:Manga": |
      Single manga by id; throws if it does not exist.
    "getMangaByIdAsFlow(id: Long) -> manga:Flow<Manga>": |
      Reactive equivalent of getMangaById.
    "getMangaByUrlAndSourceId(url: String, sourceId: Long) -> manga:Manga?": |
      Single manga matching a source-provided url within one source, or null if not present
      locally yet; the standard way a freshly-fetched SManga is resolved to a local Manga.
    "getMangaByUrlAndSourceIdAsFlow(url: String, sourceId: Long) -> manga:Flow<Manga?>": |
      Reactive equivalent of getMangaByUrlAndSourceId.
    "getFavorites() -> manga:List<Manga>": |
      Every manga currently in the user's library.
    "getReadMangaNotInLibrary() -> manga:List<Manga>": |
      Manga with reading history that are not (or no longer) in the library, for
      history/cleanup views.
    "getLibraryManga() -> libraryManga:List<LibraryManga>": |
      Library manga joined with per-manga chapter/category aggregate counts, for the library
      screen.
    "getLibraryMangaAsFlow() -> libraryManga:Flow<List<LibraryManga>>": |
      Reactive equivalent of getLibraryManga.
    "getFavoritesBySourceId(sourceId: Long) -> manga:Flow<List<Manga>>": |
      Reactive stream of library manga belonging to one source.
    "getDuplicateLibraryManga(id: Long, title: String) -> matches:List<MangaWithChapterCount>": |
      Library manga whose title closely matches `title`, excluding id itself; used to warn
      the user before adding a likely duplicate.
    "getUpcomingManga(statuses: Set<Long>, excludedCategories: List<Long>, includedCategories: List<Long>) -> manga:Flow<List<Manga>>": |
      Library manga with a future expectedNextUpdate, filtered by publication `statuses` and
      by category inclusion/exclusion, for the upcoming-releases calendar.
    "resetViewerFlags() -> succeeded:Boolean": |
      Clear viewerFlags on every manga; false if the underlying write failed.
    "setMangaCategories(mangaId: Long, categoryIds: List<Long>)": |
      Replace the full set of categories a manga belongs to.
    "update(update: MangaUpdate) -> succeeded:Boolean": |
      Apply one sparse partial update; false if the underlying write failed.
    "updateAll(mangaUpdates: List<MangaUpdate>) -> succeeded:Boolean": |
      Apply many sparse partial updates as a single unit of work; false if the write failed.
    "insertNetworkManga(manga: List<Manga>) -> inserted:List<Manga>": |
      Insert manga freshly discovered from a source, returning them with database-assigned ids
      populated.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  Storage port for the manga aggregate. Implemented by data/manga; the LibraryManga
  projection type used by getLibraryManga/getLibraryMangaAsFlow belongs to a sibling
  library-domain cell not documented in this forest (out of scope; a straightforward composition
  of Manga with aggregate counts).
